## 5. WebSocket & STOMP Flow Design

### Endpoint Configuration:
- STOMP Endpoint: `/ws` (with SockJS fallback and JWT Handshake Interceptor).
- Message Application Prefix: `/app`
- Broker Prefixes: `/topic`, `/queue`

### Channels:
1. `/topic/group/{groupId}/chat`: Real-time group chat messages.
   - Sender sends to: `/app/chat.send`
2. `/topic/group/{groupId}/typing`: Live typing indicators.
   - Sender sends to: `/app/chat.typing`
3. `/topic/group/{groupId}/events`: Real-time group events (new resource uploaded, announcement posted, AI summary completed).
4. `/topic/user/{userId}/notifications`: Personal live notifications.

### `@AI` Assistant Sequence Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Student
    participant FE as React Frontend
    participant WS as Spring Boot WebSocket Controller
    participant AI_Client as Backend AIServiceClient
    participant FastAPI as FastAPI AI Microservice
    participant DB as PostgreSQL DB

    Student->>FE: Types "@AI Explain Normalization" in group chat
    FE->>WS: STOMP send to /app/chat.send {groupId, content: "@AI..."}
    WS->>DB: Save user message to chat_messages
    WS-->>FE: Broadcast user message to /topic/group/{groupId}/chat
    
    WS->>WS: Detect "@AI" prefix in message
    WS->>FE: Broadcast typing status for "AI Assistant"
    
    WS->>AI_Client: Call askAiInGroup(groupId, question)
    AI_Client->>FastAPI: POST /ai/chat {question, document_id}
    FastAPI-->>AI_Client: Return {answer, sources}
    
    AI_Client->>DB: Save AI response message (sender = AI Assistant, type = AI_RESPONSE)
    AI_Client->>WS: Send AI message to Broker
    WS-->>FE: Broadcast AI answer to /topic/group/{groupId}/chat
```

